flowchart TB
  accTitle: Proposed B4 intention lifecycle
  accDescr: A proposed intention moves from proposed to authorized and active. A validated trigger moves it to reconsideration pending, where the governor may continue, switch method, delegate, suspend, or abandon. Satisfaction and impossibility require evidence and are terminal for this intention version.
  P[PROPOSED] -->|goal authority approves| A[AUTHORIZED]
  A -->|initial method passes checks| X[ACTIVE]
  X -->|validated trigger or scheduled review| R[RECONSIDERATION PENDING]
  R -->|continue| X
  R -->|switch method; preserve goal version| X
  R -->|delegate bounded child| D[DELEGATED]
  D -->|child result revalidated| R
  X -->|pause with resume condition| S[SUSPENDED]
  R -->|pause with resume condition| S
  S -->|resume condition satisfied| X
  X -->|verified goal success| SAT[SATISFIED]
  R -->|verified goal success| SAT
  X -->|evidence proves impossible| IMP[IMPOSSIBLE]
  R -->|evidence proves impossible| IMP
  X -->|authorized abandonment| AB[ABANDONED]
  R -->|authorized abandonment| AB
  S -->|authorized abandonment| AB
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef output fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef caution fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E
  class P,A,X source
  class R,D,S process
  class SAT output
  class IMP,AB caution
